<title>LUXEMBOURG: Finland says fulfills all EMU criteria.</title>
<headline>Finland says fulfills all EMU criteria.</headline>
<dateline>LUXEMBOURG 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish Finance Minister Sauli Niinisto said on Monday Finland was now fulfilling all of the criteria for EU economic and monetary union (EMU) following Saturday's decision to link the markka to the exchange rate mechanism (ERM).</p>
<p>&quot;We are now fulfilling all the criteria,&quot; he told a news conference at an EU finance ministers meeting in Luxembourg.  </p>
<p>Explaining why Finland had decided to join the currency grid, Niinisto said it had become more obvious since last Spring that a formal ERM link was a criterion for the third phase of EMU.</p>
<p>He said the decision would bring even more stability to the Finnish economy as well as more confidence.</p>
<p>&quot;We are quite satisfied with the rate,&quot; he said. Finland joined the ERM at a central rate of 3.04 to the German mark.</p>
<p>BRUSSELS NEWSROOM: +32 2 287-6830</p>
